-- title:
--   Constant field extension of a separably generated function field
-- statement:
--   Let $K, F, K', F'$ be fields with algebra structures $K \to F$, $K' \to F'$, $K \to K'$, $F \to F'$ and $K \to F'$, the last compatible with the towers $K \to K' \to F'$ and $K \to F \to F'$, and suppose $K$ is algebraically closed. Assume: (i) there is $x \in F$ transcendental over $K$ such that $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(x) \subseteq F$ generated by $x$; (ii) there is $x \in F'$ transcendental over $K'$ such that $F'$ is finite-dimensional over $K'(x) \subseteq F'$; (iii) the intermediate field of $F'/K'$ generated over $K'$ by the image of $F$ under $F \to F'$ is all of $F'$. Then there exists $t' \in F'$ such that $F'$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K'(t') \subseteq F'$ and $F'$ is separable over $K'(t')$.
--
--   This is the statement that a constant field extension $F' = K' \cdot F$ of a one-variable function field over an algebraically closed constant field is again separably generated, the witness being the image of a separating transcendental downstairs. It is used in the construction of places of $F'$ restricting to a prescribed place of $F$ ([`AlgebraicCurve.Place.exists_comap_algebraMap_eq_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Place.exists_comap_algebraMap_eq_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed)).
